Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 22:28:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08035/11362] The gate is right on four of five; on tn36 it is
 right with the wrong label

Force-admitting each rejected world model at its live induction point, with every
gate skipped and the plan handed to the live planner and executor, moved 0 of 9
admit cells: zero banked levels, zero change in actions-to-first-solve. Seven of
nine traces are byte-identical to their matched control, so the gate cost nothing
there. No gate change is proposed -- the two cells that produced plans banked
nothing, and widening on plan count would be the lower-the-bar anti-pattern.

ft09/tu93/lp85/sc25 are correct rejections on their own evidence: a 1112-of-1144
line comment-wall runaway whose engine() never returns; two engines at 0/8 held-out
with zero cell recall; an engine getting 0 of 2 real changes right while inventing
96 cells; and a hardcoded per-action delta lookup with a constant-False win
predicate. tn36 is REASON_IMPRECISE, not a false rejection: its engine is the run's
best (8/8 held-out, cell recall 1.0, and on force-admit its 61-action plan matched
reality byte-exactly for 61 of 61 steps), but the search was stopped by the DEPTH
cap, not degeneracy, and plan_in_model is bounded at the same depth 40 -- so the
veto is correct and only the label and detail string are wrong. It banked nothing
regardless, because the induced win predicate is not tn36's real win condition.

Two method corrections were applied before trusting any verdict. The first-pass
probes called e3.plan_in_model directly with no goal_energy, running plain BFS
while the shipped accept path runs _call_plan_in_model; every cell was re-run
through the shipped wrapper via the repo's own CARNOT_ARC_PLAN_MAX_NODES override,
and the identical node counts now measure rather than assume that a flat binary
goal energy degenerates to FIFO. The control arm was an unvalidated reconstruction;
it is now byte-identical to the live LLM-ON cell on all five games at budget 60,
with vc33 as the internal consistency check. vc33 also supplies the previously
missing positive control: 2 banked levels, a2fs 15, same harness, same inert
proposer.

Rejection reasons are now read per cell rather than per game -- tn36 and lp85 each
have a replicate rejected for a different reason, so the false-rejection claim
rests on at most 1 of 10 cells -- and sc25's terminal label is a generation
failure, so it is not a terminal gate rejection. The prior "artifact-integrity
inconsistency" is withdrawn: arc_competition_agent.py:5889 re-runs induce() after
the refinement loop returns unplanned, so a terminal event legitimately mixes
round-level fields with the post-fallthrough engine's gate fields.

Also surfaced: the TTT prior is gated on cell_recall >= 0.5 while the LLM engine is
gated on byte-exact 1.0, and on tu93 the prior PASSES at held-out exact accuracy
0.0 -- a live false positive inside the audited cells. On tn36 a gate-PASSING prior
reached the planner and the planner exhausted 20017 nodes, so tn36 is planner-bound.

The frontier is induction quality, goal induction especially, not the gate. Banked
levels remain 3/3 and the submission gate remains unmet.

